 ### [Stackless Traversal](5202-stackless-traversal.md)
-Stackless Traversal is a ray traversal algorithm for hierarchical volume structures (such as N3-trees or octrees) that eliminates the need for an explicit stack data structure by recalculating Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) parameters at every descent and ascent step. It solves the memory and register pressure issues associated with stack-based traversal on GPUs, where dynamic array indexing can force data into slow local memory. It sets itself apart from [DDA Tree Traversal with Mini-Stack](5244-dda-tree-traversal-with-mini-stack.md) by trading computational cost (repeated DDA calculations) for reduced memory footprint and avoidance of stack overflow or complex stack management logic.
